BT 1 0 0 1 0 222 Tm /F2 12 Tf 18 TL .952444 Tw (A company's e-mail gateway has quarantined an attachment named invoice_update.exe) Tj T* 0 Tw .445867 Tw (that the finance team says they did not expect. The SOC must decide quickly whether it) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.525143 Tw (is malicious and what to do. Evaluate the basics of malware analysis for this sample.) Tj T* 0 Tw .891333 Tw (Explain static analysis \(file hashing, checking the hash on reputation services, file type) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.215636 Tw (and header inspection, strings, packers, imports\) and dynamic analysis \(behaviour in a) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.501333 Tw (sandbox such as Cuckoo or Any.Run, and monitoring of processes, files, registry and) Tj T* 0 Tw .413846 Tw (network traffic with tools such as Process Monitor and Wireshark\), and describe how to) Tj T* 0 Tw .517455 Tw (set up a safe analysis laboratory \(isolated virtual machine, snapshots, host-only network) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.504571 Tw (and no shared folders\). Explain how the indicators found are extracted and fed to the) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.277333 Tw (TIP, SIEM, firewall and endpoint tools. Evaluate the limits of these methods, for) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.492 Tw (example packed or encrypted code, sandbox-aware malware that delays or hides its) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.156 Tw (actions, and false verdicts from a single vendor, and recommend how the SOC should) Tj T* 0 Tw (handle them.) Tj T* ET
